# Every variable this repository reads, and nothing it does not (I34).
#
# **Nine of these were missing and two of them stop production from starting.**
# `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` and `CHAT_TRANSPORT` default to `development`, and both
# adapters refuse to construct when `NODE_ENV=production` — so a deployment that
# followed the old version of this file exactly would fail at boot, with an
# error naming a variable the file never mentioned.
#
# `tests/i34-deployment.test.ts` now compares this file against every
# `process.env` read in the repository, in both directions. It cannot drift
# again without a test failing.
#
# **R** marks what a production deployment must set. Everything else has a
# working default and is here so its existence is discoverable.

# ─── Runtime ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# R  `production` turns on the refusals below. Anything else is a development
#    posture and the platform says so rather than pretending otherwise.
NODE_ENV=development

API_HOST=0.0.0.0
API_PORT=4000
LOG_LEVEL=info

# ─── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# R  The managed Postgres connection string. Vercel does not host this; the
#    Owner chose a managed instance on 2026-08-24.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://commerce:commerce@localhost:5432/commerce

# How many PostgreSQL connections one process may hold. Instances times this
# must stay under the server's max_connections, less the superuser reserve and
# whatever the migration job needs. A managed Postgres on a small plan often
# allows far fewer connections than this default assumes.
DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10

# The database dependency's timeout behaviour, required by Engineering
# Constitution section 13. A cancelled statement and an exhausted pool both
# answer 503 DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE rather than hanging or reporting a defect.
DATABASE_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
DATABASE_IDLE_TRANSACTION_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
DATABASE_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_MS=2000

# ─── How the three services find each other ───────────────────────────────────

# R  Where the web application reaches the API. Server-side only: the browser
#    never calls the API directly, so this must not become a NEXT_PUBLIC_ value.
#    On Vercel this points at wherever the API is hosted, which is not Vercel —
#    NestJS is a long-running process and Vercel runs functions.
API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/v1

# R  Origins allowed to establish or use a cookie session, comma separated.
#    Every login is refused from anywhere else, so this must list the real web
#    origin. The API refuses to start in production without it.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# R  Base address the emailed registration and recovery links point at. A wrong
#    value here sends every new account a link to somewhere else.
PUBLIC_WEB_URL=http://localhost:3000

# How long the web application waits for the API before answering 504 itself
# (I25). A limit rather than a prediction.
API_TIMEOUT_MS=10000

# ─── Email delivery ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# R  `development` writes to the log and **refuses to construct when
#    NODE_ENV=production**. `postmark` is the vendor adapter the Owner chose.
#    Leaving this unset in production is one of the two boot failures this file
#    used to cause by omission.
EMAIL_TRANSPORT=development

# R (when EMAIL_TRANSPORT is not `development`) — boot fails with
#    EMAIL_API_KEY_MISSING or EMAIL_SENDER_MISSING rather than turning every
#    registration into a retry nobody is watching.
EMAIL_API_KEY=
EMAIL_SENDER=

EMAIL_TIMEOUT_MS=10000

# ─── Decision Chat ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# R  Same terms as email. `development` restates the brief and adds nothing, and
#    refuses to construct in production. `anthropic` is the vendor adapter the
#    Owner chose on 2026-08-17.
CHAT_TRANSPORT=development

# R (when CHAT_TRANSPORT is not `development`) — the key and the model are named
#    separately because having one without the other is the likelier mistake,
#    and one error saying "something is missing" makes an operator guess which.
CHAT_API_KEY=
CHAT_MODEL=

CHAT_TIMEOUT_MS=8000

# ─── Observability ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The scrape token for /metrics, required by Engineering Constitution section
# 12.2. A Prometheus scraper cannot hold an Admin session, so it presents this
# as a bearer token; a person who has entered Admin context needs no token.
# Unset means no token is accepted and only the Admin context opens the
# endpoint, which never publishes it by accident.
METRICS_TOKEN=
